<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Las Navas de Tolosa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1212">1212</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Las Navas de Tolosa · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Las Navas de Tolosa was fought in 1212 in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad Caliphate</a> and a coalition of the Christian kingdoms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>, Aragon, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a> and Portugal, assembled under a papal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> declaration. The Almohad army was shattered and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-al-nasir">Muhammad al-Nasir</a> fled the field. The defeat is treated as the decisive turning point after which Muslim political power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> entered terminal decline.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-las-navas-de-tolosa.jpg" alt="Battle of Las Navas de Tolosa" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francisco de Paula Van Halen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Batalla_de_las_Navas_de_Tolosa,_por_Francisco_van_Halen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
